Phew. Finally ascended.

I started playing about half a year ago, at first trying Knights, then from
time to time Samurais and Valkyries, with the odd Wizard inbetween. Once I
got to the plane of Air with a Valkyrie who was thoroughly underprepared.

I don't remember too much of the early game, but I found an armor shop on
dlvl 1 or 2 which had a cloak of protection and Gauntlets of power, but the
cloak got lost to a polytrap accident, after my first blessed smoky potion
gozt me some GDSM, which I kept for the rest of the game.
That polytrapaccident also gave me the chance to lay some eggs which got me
a pet gray dragon baby (only one, not more because I had no magic whistle, I
wouldn't find one the whole game) later to grow up and kill all shopkeepers
(except for Izchack) and then eat a chameleon Corpse and become a Black
Dragon. He died in the Valley of the Death.
Sokoban had a "oReflection, which was nice, but I really missed a BoH, which
I would not get until a wish from the Castle Throne. Somewhere around here I
killed a peacfull Tengu, which promptly left a corpse and gave me TC, soon
to be followed by teleportitis from a random nymph or leprechaun. Medusa
died by bashing, I digged down first and came up to Medusa, which also wore
a "oLS, and had to be bashed twice. Right after Medusa I had a close Moment
with her Titan which summoned for a time, but a !oFH got me out of that.
Sometime around here I got my protection of 10 points, I cleared some vaults
and also found a Zoo and a large Leprechaun hall. Unfortunately no Fort
Ludious this game.
The Castle was pretty easy, I struck the Drawbridge with a /oStriking and
froze the water with a /oCold and bashed everything in there to death,
#twoweaponing Excalibur and my starting Katana. Those 2 I kept for the whole
game, enchanting them up to +7 after finding a Scrollshop when retreating
back up from the Castle to find the Quest level. I must have dropped by that
via a Trapdoor. With stuff from that shop I also enchanted most of my armor
to +5, which I had gotten from the Castle Wand, along with 2 magic markers.
The Quest was no Problem what-so-ever, probably due to having -39 AC. The
Quest Nemesis went to sleep from a /oSleep and I whacked him.
Next I entered Gehemnon, which seemed pretty easy, I never had any Problems,
and the Demonlords I met died quickly (Asmodeus, Orcus, Juiblex, Beelzebub).
Vlad the Wimp died very fast, and then I went to the bottom to find the
vibrating square. After that I went for the Wizard. Getting the book was no
problem, so I returned to the square to do the invocation.
Stupid me didn't realize that the Book was Cursed and thus used up the
charges of the bell because I thought I did something wrong. Having nothing
handy to recharge the Bell, I polymorphed some scrolls, which also got me
the ?oGD i needed to find the portal on the plains. Next I went down into
the sanctum, used the insects as a shield, got the Amulet, did not rise
stylishly through the ceiling because I had used up all !oGain Level, and
went back up through Gehemnon, having digged ways between the stairs
earlier.
The Mysteric Force wasn't too bad, I got pulled back 9 times, from 49 to 49,
39 -> 39, 39 -> 40, 39 -> 39, 32 -> 33, 33 -> 33, 33 -> 34, 34 -> 35, 33 ->
33.
The Wizard showed up a few times, but I just bashed him to death, no need to
waste charges of my /oDeath.
Plane of Earth was easy, confuse myself with a forgotten spell, read a ?oGD,
use /oDigging to get to the Portal. Air was similar, put on a =oLev,
confuse, read ?oGD, go to Portal. A few Air Elementals died to one of
/oDeath, zapped from the inside. Water and Fire were easy, too, though the
purple As that showed up scared me for a moment, but they were peaceful. On
Astral I started a bit to the left, so I went left. Again used the insects
as a shield, shot Famine once with the /oDeath, killed some Angels and then
